---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Reports"
	eyebrow="[ 07 · EVIDENCE ]"
	description="One SecurityReport object — two export formats that always agree."
>
	<h2>SecurityReport</h2>
	<p>
		Canonical schema <code>schemaVersion: "1.0.0"</code>. Built from an
		<code>AuditRun</code> (scan + ChaosReport) by <code>security_report.ts</code>.
	</p>

	<ul>
		<li>Target info (contract, network, bytecode size)</li>
		<li>Scan summary (functions / UDTs)</li>
		<li>Findings with signal, severity, KYF IDs</li>
		<li>Severity / signal counts</li>
		<li>Execution evidence (below)</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Execution evidence</h2>
	<p>So claims can be checked without trusting Kuyfi’s own word:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Run-wide counters: vectors executed, broadcasts, txs with hash.
		</li>
		<li>
			Per finding: simulation failed?, broadcast?, parsed DiagnosticEvent trace.
		</li>
		<li>
			If broadcast: <code>transactionHash</code>, <code>ledger</code>, stellar.expert URL.
		</li>
		<li>
			<code>verificationTransactions</code>: small deterministic sample — first successful
			broadcast and first failed broadcast (not a full dump).
		</li>
	</ul>

	<Callout type="info" title="Not every finding has a tx">
		<p>
			Simulation failures are classified from diagnostics and never sent. Only broadcast
			transactions can be independently verified on-chain.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2>Export</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Format</th>
				<th>How</th>
				<th>Notes</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td>JSON</td>
				<td>TUI <code>[J]</code> / CLI <code>--json</code></td>
				<td>Machine-readable; CI-friendly</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>PDF</td>
				<td>TUI <code>[P]</code> / CLI <code>--pdf</code></td>
				<td>pdfkit render; labeled as automated black-box, not a formal audit</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Both</td>
				<td>TUI <code>[B]</code> / <code>--json --pdf</code></td>
				<td>Same underlying <code>report_export.ts</code></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<pre><code>kuyfi C… --json --pdf
# writes SecurityReport JSON + PDF from the identical object</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
